-- title:
--   Characters of the Hecke algebra come from normalised eigenforms
-- statement:
--   Fix a level $N$ with $N \neq 0$ and work in weight $2$. Assume the project hypothesis [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6), which says that the complex span of the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule [`CuspForm.intLattice N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L3) of $S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ is everything, where that submodule is the $\mathbb{Z}$-span of the cusp forms all of whose $q$-expansion coefficients [`ModularFormClass.qCoeff`](def/FLTPrelim_Modularity.html#L19) (coefficients of `qExpansion 1`) are rational integers. Let $S \subseteq \mathbb{N}$ be an arbitrary set of naturals, and let $\chi$ be a ring homomorphism from [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) to $\mathbb{C}$; here [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) is the $\mathbb{Z}$-subalgebra of $\operatorname{End}_{\mathbb{C}}(S_2(\Gamma_0(N)))$ generated by the operators [`CuspForm.heckeTLin`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperatorForms.html#L69) for primes $\ell \nmid N$ with $\ell \notin S$ together with the operators [`CuspForm.heckeULin`](def/ModularForm_HeckeOperatorForms.html#L83) for primes $q \mid N$ with $q \notin S$, so that the primes in $S$ are omitted. The conclusion is that there exists a cusp form $f \in S_2(\Gamma_0(N))$ such that: (i) $f$ satisfies the project predicate [`CuspForm.IsNormalizedEigenform`](def/FLTPrelim_Modularity.html#L28), i.e. its coefficients $a_n =$ `qCoeff f n` satisfy $a_1 = 1$, $a_{mn} = a_m a_n$ for coprime $m,n$, $a_{p^{r+2}} = a_p a_{p^{r+1}} - p\,a_{p^r}$ for primes $p \nmid N$ and $a_{p^{r+2}} = a_p a_{p^{r+1}}$ for primes $p \mid N$; (ii) $a_\ell = \chi(\mathrm{T}_\ell)$ for every prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$ and $\ell \notin S$, where $\mathrm{T}_\ell$ is [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.T`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L77); and (iii) $a_q = \chi(\mathrm{U}_q)$ for every prime $q$ with $q \mid N$ and $q \notin S$, where $\mathrm{U}_q$ is [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.U`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L80). Nothing is asserted about the coefficients of $f$ at primes belonging to $S$, and no uniqueness of $f$ is claimed.
--
--   This is the existence half of the dictionary between complex characters of the weight-two Hecke algebra and normalised eigenforms, in the style of Deligne–Serre and of the integral Hecke-algebra discussion in Diamond–Shurman. Two features distinguish it from the textbook statement: the integrality input is taken as the hypothesis [`CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2`](def/CuspForm_IntegralStructure.html#L6) rather than proved, and the normalisation property is the project's coefficient-level predicate [`CuspForm.IsNormalizedEigenform`](def/FLTPrelim_Modularity.html#L28) (multiplicativity plus the prime-power recursions), while $\chi$ pins down the coefficients of $f$ only at primes outside $S$ — at primes of $S$ the eigenvalues of $f$ are unconstrained. It is used to convert a character of a Hecke algebra into an eigenform: in the passage from maximal ideals of [`CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 ∅`](def/CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra.html#L18) to normalised eigenforms, and in the statements attaching Galois representations and Tate-module eigenplanes to newforms.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_CuspForm_HasIntegralStructure_exists_isNormalizedEigenform_qCoeff_eq.lean

import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_HeckeAlgebra
import Definitions.Def_CuspForm_IntegralStructure

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
set_option synthInstance.maxHeartbeats 400000
set_option backward.isDefEq.respectTransparency.types false

theorem CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure.exists_isNormalizedEigenform_qCoeff_eq {N : ℕ} [NeZero N] (hN : CuspForm.HasIntegralStructure N 2) {S : Set ℕ} (χ : CuspForm.heckeAlgebra N 2 S →+* ℂ) : ∃ f : CuspForm (CongruenceSubgroup.Gamma0 N) 2, f.IsNormalizedEigenform ∧ (∀ (ℓ : ℕ) (hℓ : ℓ.Prime) (hℓN : ¬ ℓ ∣ N) (hℓS : ℓ ∉ S), ModularFormClass.qCoeff f ℓ = χ (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.T hℓ hℓN hℓS)) ∧ ∀ (q : ℕ) (hq : q.Prime) (hqN : q ∣ N) (hqS : q ∉ S), ModularFormClass.qCoeff f q = χ (CuspForm.heckeAlgebra.U hq hqN hqS) := by sorry
